Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||07-25-2001||09:31 AM||||hey I like the umbrella option - sometimes when I stop at a light pointing south with the sunroof out, the heat is too much until I get moving again - would be nice to pop the umbrella open at a red light.<P> where did you get that - the Fiero Store?! do they come in silver or green only.<P> I was riding around yesterday reaching my hand out the drivers window and up over the roof. Right near the roof at the back window it felt like the air was moving forwards at 55mph. about 8 to 12" above the roof at the back edge is where the max backwards airflow was.<P>   Anyone ever try to put an air scoop under the car?! We need to get a pressure sensor to do these kinds of tests.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||Oreif||07-25-2001||09:04 PM||||The reason many racecars don't put scoops down low is the air just above the road's surface is hotter than the air above a car. This heat is what looks like water on the road when you look down a long highway. Usually it looks "wavy" just above the horizon. As for keeping the scoop the same height but lowering the roof, I don't think the it would make much different at low speeds. At the higher highway speeds it may make a slight difference. You could take a pic of your car and a pick of the scoop then "raise" the scoop with photo-editing software on a computer to see if you like how it looks.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||07-27-2001||12:37 PM||||Who would use "photo editing" software to modify a photo?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
